          "requirement": "Exercise the supported pre-parse operation that sets an explicit 16-byte hash salt for the parsers this target creates and parses.",
          "target_route": "LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput creates root and external parsers; each ParseOneInput calls XML_SetHashSalt before XML_Parse.",
          "failure_condition": "For any target input, the explicit setter is never called. The invoked legacy setter writes zero to the first 64-bit key half, so it cannot supply an explicit 16-byte key with a nonzero first half.",
          "alternative_paths": "Automatic generation may create a full-width key when the salt remains unset, but it does not exercise caller-supplied 16-byte entropy. Child parsers inherit the parent's salt and are passed through the same legacy setter; neither route is equivalent.",
          "discovery_necessary": true,
          "discovery_established": true
        }
      ],
      "decisions": [
        {
